                            "niechęć, żal do kogoś"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5c71f857-6aa8-4b36-9793-0ac692bd55f9",
                        "source_entry_id": "e5194aba-1c24-379c-81a1-d5ccc7670933",
                        "source_sense_id": "a0e51bc2-6c9c-3da6-a433-917aad64803f",
                        "target_lang_word": "grudge",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "grudge",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7e3abd29-e9db-38c5-adda-111fbe54a0e3",
                                        "entry_id": "9766cfca-e185-32ba-b5ef-8a977b003290",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Deep-seated and/or long-term animosity or ill will about something or someone, especially due to perceived mistreatment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e987760-2eaa-42e9-9b98-8044b434ea0b",
                                                "sense_id": "7e3abd29-e9db-38c5-adda-111fbe54a0e3",
                                                "text": "to have, hold, or bear a grudge against someone"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c090044-e9c2-4a14-9c82-08bf500b4ce0",
                                                "sense_id": "7e3abd29-e9db-38c5-adda-111fbe54a0e3",
                                                "text": "Bag. And if I do not my good Lord damme me for it\nI haue an old grudge at him cole black curre,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "951fa6de-29be-43e7-b901-771a1cd8d47f",
                                                "sense_id": "7e3abd29-e9db-38c5-adda-111fbe54a0e3",
                                                "text": "I have never mentioned it to a human creature; I have kept my grudge to myself. I daresay I have been wicked, but my grudge has grown old with me."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51367910-6868-4bed-881a-98367103d71c",
                                                "sense_id": "7e3abd29-e9db-38c5-adda-111fbe54a0e3",
                                                "text": "It is towards Saduko that he bears a grudge, for you know, my father, one should never pull a drowning man out of the stream — which is what Saduko did, for had it not been for his treachery, Cetewayo would have sunk beneath the water of Death — especially if it is only to spite a woman who hates him."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "grudge",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bb34a84c-9a31-338b-a8fa-1379133bbe0d",
                                        "entry_id": "32cbaa5b-4430-3b1e-9d7c-125eea328908",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To be unwilling to give or allow (someone something)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5fd433a-08ae-4932-832d-e8304f2e0058",
                                                "sense_id": "bb34a84c-9a31-338b-a8fa-1379133bbe0d",
                                                "text": "Wee shall finde our whole life so necessarily ioyned with sorrow, that we ought rather delight (and take pleasure) in Gods louing chastisements, and admonitions, then any way murmure and grudge at our crosses, or tribulations :"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5428323f-3106-4c32-b8c1-8f6c6742c7ec",
                                                "sense_id": "bb34a84c-9a31-338b-a8fa-1379133bbe0d",
                                                "text": "If we of the central land were to grudge you what is beneficial, and not to compassionate your wants, then wherewithal could you foreigners manage to exist?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "337e4377-d692-4629-abed-e2fa58423c6c",
                                                "sense_id": "bb34a84c-9a31-338b-a8fa-1379133bbe0d",
                                                "text": "Of course, his interest in the war and in the regiment was unbounded; he did not take to drill with especial readiness, but he was insatiable of it, and grudged every moment of relaxation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49474be3-bc5c-473a-b12e-024aa688b90d",
                                                "sense_id": "bb34a84c-9a31-338b-a8fa-1379133bbe0d",
                                                "text": "Our two inimitable drolls did a roaring trade with their broadsheets among lovers of the comedy element and nobody who has a corner in his heart for real Irish fun without vulgarity will grudge them their hardearned pennies."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11bddf93-c2bb-4b3c-b7c2-f7c1681148d3",
                                                "sense_id": "bb34a84c-9a31-338b-a8fa-1379133bbe0d",
                                                "text": "I've never seen such people for borrowing and lending; there was dough changing hands in all directions, and nobody grudged anyone."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c7023b27-4ed8-36f9-bd92-5233688a4c4e",
                                        "entry_id": "32cbaa5b-4430-3b1e-9d7c-125eea328908",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To grumble, complain; to be dissatisfied."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f86e484b-f3b1-4050-aa25-0bb481bc9435",
                                                "sense_id": "c7023b27-4ed8-36f9-bd92-5233688a4c4e",
                                                "text": "And the pharises, and scribes grudged sainge: He receaveth to his company synners [...]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c314939f-e89d-32b2-89c2-663f458d1ff6",
                                        "entry_id": "32cbaa5b-4430-3b1e-9d7c-125eea328908",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To hold or harbour with malicious disposition or purpose; to cherish enviously."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "784a5f1a-922c-4884-91ed-24242584a738",
                                                "sense_id": "c314939f-e89d-32b2-89c2-663f458d1ff6",
                                                "text": "Perish they / That grudge one thought against your majesty!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a65cdf9a-7367-4492-bfa2-429d40c7232c",
                        "source_entry_id": "e5194aba-1c24-379c-81a1-d5ccc7670933",
                        "source_sense_id": "a0e51bc2-6c9c-3da6-a433-917aad64803f",
                        "target_lang_word": "rancune",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rancune",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "63aea732-bc78-3233-94a9-4eb1ec063d7a",
                                        "entry_id": "6b6cf398-d99d-3b34-b9ab-737e0fd2d772",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ressentiment tenace, sentiment profond de mal-être, opinion négative envers quelqu’un suite à du mal, des offenses subies."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48218bef-ba63-4ce3-a76e-454201e670b3",
                                                "sense_id": "63aea732-bc78-3233-94a9-4eb1ec063d7a",
                                                "text": "Le gros Léon, se montrant plus généreux, avait généralement de meilleurs tuyaux que son confrère, lequel, en secret, lui gardait bien un peu rancune de la chose."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "631e19f0-2df8-4670-8eb8-db7498d650da",
                                                "sense_id": "63aea732-bc78-3233-94a9-4eb1ec063d7a",
                                                "text": "La Pauvreté, ah! la garce! Elle va dans un cortège d'humiliations, de basses rancunes, de fangeuses abdications. Elle traîne, derrière elle, sa sœur la Misère, au rire édenté, aux orbites desséchées, aux doigts mous."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d1c1dda-c035-408b-aa92-089be0fa02c3",
                                                "sense_id": "63aea732-bc78-3233-94a9-4eb1ec063d7a",
                                                "text": "Il m’arrivait de ne pouvoir retenir une moquerie qui les blessait mortellement et dont ils me gardaient rancune."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "rancune",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f7172e60-32db-3f69-8fce-0c71cae18fc6",
